<title>USA: PXRE current Q3 includes $3.0 mln.</title>
<headline>PXRE current Q3 includes $3.0 mln.</headline>
<dateline>EDISON, N.J. 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>PXRE Corp said Wednesday that its loss ratio for the third quarter of 1996 primarily reflected $3.0 million of incurred losses from Hurricane Fran.</p>
<p>In the third quarter of 1995, the company incurred losses of $11.0 million from Hurricanes Marilyn and Luis which was offset by a reduction in incurred losses for the Kobe earthquake of $3.0 million.</p>
<p>The loss ratio for the nine months ended September 30, 1996, reflected $2.8 million of loss development on Hurricanes Marilyn and Luis in addition to the $3.0 million of incurred losses for Hurricane Fran, it said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
